# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WeVolunteer — CLIENT build-time configuration (template)
#
#   cp .env.production.example .env.production   # then edit, then `npm run build`
#
# `vite build` reads `.env.production` automatically. These values are BAKED
# INTO THE BUNDLE at build time — setting them on the running server does
# nothing. Change any of them and you must rebuild and redeploy.
#
# Nothing here is secret: every value ends up in JavaScript the browser
# downloads. Never put an API key, a database path, or JWT_SECRET in this file.
# Server-side secrets belong in the systemd EnvironmentFile — see
# docs/operations/pilot-deployment-runbook.md §5.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Privacy notice ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH.
#
# WeVolunteer stores identifying information about minors — name, grade,
# school, email address — and shows some of it to organizers whose events a
# student applies to.
#
# When this is set, the signup form shows a required acknowledgement checkbox
# linking to it. When it is unset, that control does not render at all (Vite
# removes the block from the bundle), so the app collects this data with no
# disclosure and no consent record.
#
# This is deliberately empty. The URL must point at a privacy notice the
# district has actually reviewed and published. Do not point it at a
# placeholder page: a consent checkbox linking to nothing is worse than no
# checkbox, because it manufactures the appearance of a reviewed policy.
#
# The document itself is a district deliverable, not an engineering one. It
# needs to cover, at minimum:
#   - what is collected (name, email, grade, school, service hours)
#   - who can see it (the student, administrators, and organizers of events
#     the student applied to; opt-in leaderboard shows name + hours to all
#     signed-in users)
#   - how long it is retained
#   - how a family requests correction or deletion, and who to contact
#   - whether under-13 signups are in scope and what consent applies
#
VITE_PRIVACY_URL=


# ── Public origin printed on certificates ────────────────────────────────────
#
# Optional. The origin shown on a printed certificate as the place to verify
# it ("Verify at <host>/verify/WEV-XXXX-XXXX").
#
# Leave blank unless certificates are printed from somewhere other than the
# public address. Blank means the app uses the origin the page was served
# from, which is correct for a normal deployment.
#
VITE_PUBLIC_URL=


# ── Branding ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Defaults shown.
#
# VITE_APP_NAME=WeVolunteer
# VITE_SCHOOL_NAME=South Brunswick, NJ


# ── Feature switches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Set to false to remove the community leaderboard entirely. It is already
# opt-in per student and default-off; this is the belt-and-braces option if the
# district would rather it not exist at all.
#
# VITE_ENABLE_LEADERBOARD=false


# ── Never set in production ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# VITE_DEMO_MODE exposes one-click sign-in as seeded demo accounts, including an
# administrator, using a password published in the README. It lives only in
# `.env.development`, which `vite build` does not read. Do not add it here.
